      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b7701d21379b741ac2719d8|full_name}: If people make avatars from scatch there is no need to reduce the limitin VRC. You can create a normal map from hi-poly models and apply these to a low poly version. Looks the same since VR is not 4K at least ot yet I couldnt tell the difference. The problem are MMDs and other ripped stuff thats already hi poly. Optimizing these is often harder than building a new one.",
      "viewerReactions": null
